==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*kʷyeh₁-}}
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*pokojь}}.

{{sense|apartment, room, chamber}} Compare typologically {{m+|gem-pro|*razną}} (whence {{m+|en|ransack}}) (possibly from {{m+|ine-pro|*h₁reh₁-||to rest}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|поко́й}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-покой.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-покой.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|поко́й|par=поко́ю}}

# [[calm]], [[rest]], [[peace]]
# [[quiet]]
# old name of the letter '''[[п#Russian|п]]''' in the early Cyrillic alphabet
# [[apartment]], [[room]], [[chamber]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[приёмный поко́й]]|[[admission department]], [[admission room]] {{gloss|in a hospital}}}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[поко́и]] [[императрица|императри́цы]]|living or private chambers of the [[empress]]}}

